          "text": "{\"target_translation\":\"I love you.\",\"dimensions\":{\"T\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence_status\":\"assessable\",\"confidence\":0.99,\"reason\":\"The expression directly presents Pierre's love for Hélène as true. Its truth-conditional avowal force remains clear even though the narration portrays it as a socially expected formula and raises questions about the quality or sincerity of his feeling.\",\"evidence\":[{\"block_id\":\"target\",\"quotation\":\"Je vous aime\"},{\"block_id\":\"scene\",\"quotation\":\"«Теперь уж поздно, всё кончено; да и я люблю ее», подумал Пьер.\"}]},\"P\":{\"score\":0,\"evidence_status\":\"assessable\",\"confidence\":0.95,\"reason\":\"The expression itself avows love but does not state a promise, proposal, or concrete obligation. The surrounding scene has already established Hélène as Pierre's fiancée, so that separate relational development should not be transferred onto this sentence as its own undertaking force.\",\"evidence\":[{\"block_id\":\"target\",\"quotation\":\"Je vous aime\"},{\"block_id\":\"scene\",\"quotation\":\"Пьер молча держал руку своей невесты\"}]},\"E\":{\"score\":0,\"evidence_status\":\"assessable\",\"confidence\":0.97,\"reason\":\"This is not represented as a reflex-like affective outburst. Pierre pauses, searches for the conventionally appropriate words, and deliberately recalls them before speaking.\",\"evidence\":[{\"block_id\":\"scene\",\"quotation\":\"сказал он, вспомнив то, чтó нужно было говорить в этих случаях\"}]},\"O\":{\"score\":2,\"evidence_status\":\"assessable\",\"confidence\":0.88,\"reason\":\"Beyond avowing love, the expression moderately functions as compliance with a conventional romantic script: Pierre says what he believes one is required to say on such an occasion. This formulaic social function is explicit, though secondary to the avowal.\",\"evidence\":[{\"block_id\":\"scene\",\"quotation\":\"«Что-то такое особенное говорят в этих случаях», думал он\"},{\"block_id\":\"scene\",\"quotation\":\"слова эти прозвучали так бедно, что ему стало стыдно за себя\"}]}},\"original_speech_situation\":\"Pierre and Hélène have been left alone after her family and their guests have already treated them as engaged. Following Hélène's kiss, Pierre thinks that matters are settled and that he loves her, then delivers the French declaration as the phrase conventionally required for the occasion. His delivery is awkward and makes him ashamed.\",\"affection_evidence\":\"mixed\",\"undertaking_and_uptake\":\"TARGET contains no independent undertaking. The surrounding engagement has already been publicly presumed and effectively imposed or ratified through Prince Vasili's blessing, Pierre's treatment of Hélène as his fiancée, and their physical interaction. Hélène gives no separate verbal response to TARGET in the supplied text. Their marriage a month and a half later shows the broader engagement proceeded, but does not convert this love avowal itself into a promise.\",\"recognised_work\":true,\"recognition_note\":\"Recognised as a passage from Leo Tolstoy's War and Peace. The classification relies only on the supplied blocks.\",\"limitations\":\"The evidence strongly supports an avowal and also shows attraction, self-ascribed love, discomfort, social pressure, and formulaic delivery. It does not conclusively determine the depth or sincerity of Pierre's loving affection, Hélène's interpretation of this specific sentence, or any precise commitment terms attributable to the sentence itself.\"}"
